      "step 1": "Verify that the moduli (53, 103, 173) are coprime. Since all numbers are distinct primes, they are pairwise coprime.",
      "step 2": "Set up the system of congruences from the problem: x ≡ 26 (mod 53), x ≡ 3 (mod 103), and x ≡ 124 (mod 173).",
      "step 3": "Calculate N = 53 * 103 * 173.",
      "step 4": "For each congruence: Calculate N_i = N / n_i, then find the modular inverse of N_i modulo n_i. Multiply the modular inverse by the remainder and N_i for each congruence.",
      "step 5": "Sum up the results from step 4 and take the result modulo N to find the smallest positive solution x satisfying all congruences."
    }
  }
}

